    "pages": [
      {
        "id": "p0",
        "title": "No Guaranteed Punish",
        "text": "RG buys you a chance to act - it does NOT guarantee a punish. The attacker can still cancel, or Recoil Counter you, while their original move recovers. Fast Light normals are usually bad places to challenge: their next cancel can win the race."
      },
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "title": "Better Targets",
        "text": "Big dash normals and Specials are much juicier targets - they have real recovery and few safe cancels. And if the attacker goes for a risky follow-up, plain blocking can beat another RG: your later punish no longer hands them a Recoil Counter."
      }
    ],
